id: interface/yawn-brand-v1
title: "YAWN brand contract v1"
kind: interface-contract
status: active
updated: 2026-08-14

purpose: >
  Give every YAWN lens the same visual meaning without making every surface
  visually identical.

colors:
  field: "#000000"
  raised: "#181716"
  text: "#ffffff"
  logo_and_primary_action: "#e8ff03"
  interaction_and_connection: "#2fe3f4"
  unresolved_lacuna: "#fd49ac"
  source_and_provenance: "#ff7300"
  resolved_or_verified: "#64ff03"

css_variables:
  --yawn-field: "#000000"
  --yawn-raised: "#181716"
  --yawn-text: "#ffffff"
  --yawn-lime: "#e8ff03"
  --yawn-cyan: "#2fe3f4"
  --yawn-pink: "#fd49ac"
  --yawn-orange: "#ff7300"
  --yawn-green: "#64ff03"

semantic_roles:
  signal_and_source: --yawn-orange
  observation_and_connection: --yawn-cyan
  proposed_interpretation: --yawn-pink
  open_or_unresolved: --yawn-lime
  correction_or_verified: --yawn-green
  note: >
    These aliases make the observation passage legible without changing the
    stable palette. Product marks and a page's one primary action may also use
    lime, but color never changes epistemic kind or authority.

rules:
  - default surfaces foreground one state and one next action with the least visible copy that preserves comprehension
  - rationale taxonomy and repeated status live behind explicit disclosure rather than beside self-explanatory controls
  - icon-only controls keep accessible names
  - color never carries state without a text or icon label
  - headings use the pixel or mono face and body copy uses a readable sans face
  - chrome uses one-pixel dividers, slim route tabs, and restrained corner radii
  - public pages do not render the authenticated sidebar
  - both public hosts consume these exact values rather than near-match literals
  - a route skin may add visual roles but cannot remap canonical semantic roles
  - the proposed yawn-64 spiral skin remains view-scoped and non-canonical until its reference is approved
  - legacy asset paths may remain aliases but are not public product identity

proof:
  acceptance:
    - host-specific title, icon, canonical URL, and wordmark
    - no visible Nestheads product branding on new public surfaces
    - keyboard focus is visible against every semantic color
